#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Germany.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The DDP prides itself as a stable, governing, democratic party. However, if we do not have sufficient relations with other parties we cannot govern.

- @liberals: Strengthen our bonds with the German Peoples Party (DVP). 
- @center: Strengthen our bonds with the Catholic Center Party.
- @socialist: Work towards further cooperation with the Socialist party(s).
- @dnvp: Attempt to repair our relations with the right-wing DNVP.
- @ddp_alone: The DDP can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@socialist
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: socialist_1 

@socialist_1
on-arrival: uspd_relation += 5*(1 - dissent); ddp_relation += 8*(1 - dissent) 

The SPD is our natural governing partner and thus repairing relations is easy.



@center
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: center_op 

@center_op
on-arrival: z_relation += 7*(1 - dissent)

We develop closer ties to Zentrum, they are very likely to be included in any government we form.


@dnvp
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: dnvp_1

@dnvp_1
on-arrival: dnvp_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We have a hard time improving relations with the anti-republican DNVP, however, some progress is made.

@liberals
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: dvp_stresemann

@dvp_stresemann
on-arrival: dvp_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

The DVP are our liberal brethren, improving relations with them is natural.


@ddp_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
